--[[
    Stun Evade / Auto Parry client - build 20
    (Infinite Force, Infinite Block, Infinite Parry/Kicks, Hitbox Expander,
     Auto Parry, Auto Evade, Anti-kick, Chase Multi, input sink)

    WHAT CHANGED IN THIS BUILD (all of it is in the notes below)
      1) INPUT SINK - "keys can't interrupt Stun Evade" (section: Input Sink)
         Every keyboard key and every mouse button is swallowed before the game can
         see it - EXCEPT RIGHT CLICK, which stays fully live (block / parry).
         Nothing is faked and no input event is mutated: a ContextActionService
         binding at priority 9000 sinks the key/button, and the game's own bindings
         are moved below it once per character. Camera, menu and script features
         still work because they read raw input or drive the game's own functions.

      2) CHASE MULTI - new toggle in the panel (section: Chase Multi)
         When YOUR parry stuns somebody you dash to where they went and multi them:
             W  ->  E (force dash, one frame later)  ->  LEFT CLICK (swing)
         and the cycle repeats on its own as fast as the game allows (it is driven by
         the saber's own animation events, not by a fixed timer).
         It stops the instant their stun animation ends, and it never presses
         anything while you hold RIGHT CLICK (so your block/parry is never broken).

      3) AUTO PARRY CHASE FIX
         The old "did the parry really start?" 80-150ms delayed click is gone, so
         nothing is queued that could fire a swing while you are chasing, and a
         "chase" flag is raised the moment a parry is sent so Chase Multi starts on
         the first stun frame instead of hunting for a target.

    The rest of the features are the ones from the previous build, kept intact.
]]

