-- Auto Parry
--   You hold right-click (saber ignited); the script presses left-click for you when
--   an incoming swing is really aimed at you.
--
--   Detection: attackers' swing animations replicate to your client, so we watch every
--   other player's Animator for one of the game's attack animations (Attack_1-4 for every
--   form + dash attacks) and read its TimePosition.
--
--   A swing is a THREAT only if it is aimed at you (facing), about to land (blade path /
--   closing speed vs your ping), and committed (not a feint). All of the tuning is in AP.
--
--   CHASE FIX (this build): the old version clicked, then waited 80-150ms to ask "did the
--   parry really start?" and clicked AGAIN if not. That second click could land while you
--   were already dashing at the stunned enemy and swing instead of parry, and it also
--   kept the parry coroutine alive long after you had moved on. It is gone: a parry is
--   sent exactly once, on the frame it is needed, through the game's own input function.
